Hi team,

The antenna rotator gearbox at Hollin Ridge is being replaced from 12 to
16 May, so the dish will be parked and unusable for the whole week. All
Mirelle-1 passes in that period move to the backup station at Saltmarsh
Point.

The shared university dish at Saltmarsh is only available to us for two
passes a day, so expect roughly a third of the usual image volume. The
imaging planners have already cut the lagoon list to match.

The same rules apply at the backup site: we only schedule passes that
peak more than 10 degrees above the horizon, and command uploads still
need a pass above 25 degrees with two people on console.

One gap remains. Pass HR-0412 on Tuesday morning has no equivalent from
Saltmarsh, so the command plan for Wednesday has to go up on Monday
evening instead.

Thanks,
Anneli
Ground segment lead
